Continue: 
- used to skip particular iteration.
- used only in loops(for/while/ do while)

eg: 
for(i = 1; i<=5; i++)
{
if(i==3)
continue;
printf("%d", i);
}

output: 1 2 4 5

eg: 
int i =1;
while(i<=5)
{
if(i ==3)
continue;
printf("%d", i);
i++;
}

output: 1 2

- in while loop,when the iteration meets the continue, it will directly go to while(condition) not the i++.

eg:
int i = 0;
do
{
i++;
if(i==2)
continue;
printf("%d", i);
}
while(i<=2);

output: 1 3

eg: 
for(i =1; i<=3; i++)
{
for(j = 1; j<=5; j++)
{
if(j ==3)
break;
printf("%d", j);
}
}

output: 1 2 1 2 1 2
